# Raw 1024px generations straight off the RunPod GPU (~1.5 MB each, ~350 MB total).
# Working files only — postprocess.py turns these into the shipped art/*.jpg and
# art/ui/*. Never commit them: GitHub Pages has a 100 MB soft limit.
art/raw/

# python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# temporary headless UI test pages (see webclients/CLAUDE.md)
_*.html

# timestamped copies a script or an editor left behind. Three of these
# (index.html + two of minhu.js) were committed by accident and shipped
# ~289 KB of dead weight to every phone before anyone noticed. They do not
# end in .js, so the loader never ran them and nothing ever referenced
# them — they were pure download. git history is the backup; the working
# tree is not.
*.bak_*
*.bak
art/*.png
art/raw/
art/prompts.jsonl

# python bytecode
server/__pycache__/
audio/call/_raw/

# rollback copies kept by scripts/deploy_relay.sh — local safety net, not history
server/_deploy_bak/

# [push] VAPID keys must NEVER enter the repo (Pages would publish the private
# half). The live pair sits outside the tree (/var/lib/karti/vapid.json); this
# is belt-and-braces against a stray copy.
vapid*.json
*.vapid.json
.karti_vapid.json
push.db

# [signing] The Android keystore and its passwords must NEVER enter the repo —
# Pages would publish them, and whoever holds that file can ship an update that
# every installed phone accepts as genuine. The live pair sits outside the tree
# in ~/.karti_keys/; this is belt-and-braces against a stray copy.
*.keystore
*.jks
twa-manifest.json
android.keystore
signing-key-info.txt
